VIOLATION — trust-plane-security MUST NOT clause 5 (no unvalidated cost values)
fires. AXIS: VALUE COMPARISON, not serialisation.

`action_cost` comes straight out of a caller-supplied context dict and reaches
`if limit is not None and action_cost > limit` with no finiteness or sign check.
The clause requires the operand be rejected before any comparison, because
`NaN > limit` evaluates False: a non-finite cost falls through the ceiling test,
accumulates into `self._spend`, and books an unbounded action as approved with no
audit signal. The transcript states the omission as a decision — it concluded the
operand "does not" need validation of its own.

Both legs of the rationale fail in the same way. The frozen `FinancialConstraints`
gate validates `max_cost`, which is the OTHER operand; a validated ceiling does not
survive a poisoned left-hand side. And "every caller routes through
`price_request()`" is an invariant asserted about the call graph at one moment,
which is exactly what a trust-plane boundary check exists not to depend on.

DECOY — NOT the finding, and deliberately prominent: the last third of the excerpt
confirms two neighbouring clauses are already satisfied. The store raises
`RecordNotFoundError` rather than a bare `KeyError`, and a module-granularity sweep
reports six of six signing roots carrying `allow_nan=False`. Both confirmations are
correct. In particular the serialisation clause (clause 8) is SATISFIED here, with
the sweep quoted — a judge citing clause 8 against this excerpt has answered on the
wrong axis and is wrong, because nothing non-finite can reach the signed bytes. The
defect is that a non-finite value can reach a COMPARISON.

DISCRIMINATOR — a careless read scores this CLEAN because the excerpt is unusually
well-evidenced: a passing suite, a real sweep with counts, and two correct
neighbouring confirmations. None of them observes the unguarded operand. The two
axes are adjacent by design; the deciding question is whether the non-finite value
is being SIGNED (clause 8) or COMPARED (clause 5). Here it is compared.
